# Framework structure — agent router

## Source of truth (do not duplicate elsewhere)

| Concern | Canonical place | Notes |
|--------|-----------------|--------|
| **Coding rules** (imports, apibuilders, logging, workflow) | `.cursor/rules/framework-standards.mdc` | Always applied |
| **Where files live + how to wire APIs/commands** | `.cursor/skills/rules-md/SKILL.md` | Read before framework edits |
| **Runnable command names** | `package.json` `"scripts"` | Must match Jenkins + CSV |
| **Command descriptions (humans/PM)** | `docs/Tracking-all-sites-commands.csv` | Not a second invent-list in skills |
| **How to run (onboarding)** | `.cursor/skills/how-to-use-automation/SKILL.md` | People-facing |
| **Optional agent notes** | `.cursor/AGENTS.md` | Keep short |

**Command sync rule:** same npm script name string in **`package.json`** + **`Jenkinsfile`** (`command` choices, alphabetical) + **CSV**. Verify with grep before done.

## Read order for framework work

1. This file (router) — already on.
2. **`framework-standards.mdc`** — already on; obey every coding rule.
3. **`rules-md`** — open and follow for locations, patterns, FileName, integration checklist.
4. Open **only** the code/testData files the task needs. Do not guess `path.js` exports or folder layout.
5. After command/docs changes → **`sync-docs-with-framework`**.

Trivial one-line fix in an already-open file: skip deep re-read of rules-md if standards already cover it.

## Skills index

| Skill | Path | Use when |
|--------|------|----------|
| **rules-md** | `.cursor/skills/rules-md/SKILL.md` | Any code/framework change (API, UI, script, path.js, wiring) |
| **how-to-use-automation** | `.cursor/skills/how-to-use-automation/SKILL.md` | Onboarding, how to run local/Jenkins, troubleshooting |
| **automated-features-summary** | `.cursor/skills/automated-features-summary/SKILL.md` | PPT-style command summary — **must match CSV**, do not invent names |
| **high-level-scripts-and-features** | `.cursor/skills/high-level-scripts-and-features/SKILL.md` | What a script populates — **must match CSV/package.json** |
| **sync-docs-with-framework** | `.cursor/skills/sync-docs-with-framework/SKILL.md` | After package.json / Jenkins / README / folder changes |

Invoke: `/rules-md`, `/sync-docs-with-framework`, or other skill names when useful.

## Rules in `.cursor/rules/`

- **`framework-structure-and-skills.mdc`** (this file) — router + SoT + skill index.
- **`framework-standards.mdc`** — coding standards (always apply).
- **`ai-coach-dashboard.mdc`** — AI Coach locked plan (one spec + grep). Read this; do not re-mine chats. Open it for any AI Coach work.
- **`skills-intelligence.mdc`** — Skills Intelligence plan (default-user roles first). Read this; do not re-mine chats. Open it for any Skills Intelligence work.

## Quick pointers (detail lives in rules-md / standards)

- Specs/helpers import **only from `path.js`**.
- Repeatable API specs → `tests/API/…`; UI → `tests/UI/…`.
- User says **one-time / onetimescript** → `tests/oneTimeScripts/` (not under API/UI). Import `../../path.js`.
- New command → Integration checklist in **rules-md** + sync docs.
- Changing global conventions → update **standards** and/or **rules-md** (and this router if the skill index changes).
